V1 — Enterprise Citizen Data Gateway

0. Mission

Evolve the existing V0 Python FastAPI application into V1 of an enterprise-grade Citizen Data Gateway.

The existing V0 is already functional and must NOT be discarded.

V0 currently proves two core capabilities:

1. Databricks/Unity Catalog authorization.
2. SQL validation and query guardrails.

V1 must preserve those capabilities and introduce:

1. Business-level access/entitlement metadata.
2. A domain/data-product semantic layer.
3. Semantic discovery from existing enterprise/Databricks metadata.
4. Pluggable query-understanding providers.
5. Databricks Genie as the initial query-understanding implementation.
6. OpenAI/enterprise LLM as a future interchangeable implementation.
7. Microsoft Graph/Entra as the future enterprise identity/group provider.
8. A source-agnostic data-source abstraction, while implementing Databricks as the only V1 physical data-source adapter.
9. Auditability.
10. Clean architectural boundaries so V2 can add SQL Server, Azure SQL, Oracle, Salesforce, APIs, etc. without redesigning the core platform.

⸻

1. Enterprise Context

The organization has approximately:

* 45,000 potential citizen developers.
* Approximately 50+ enterprise data hubs/data products.
* Approximately 50–60% of those data hubs are currently available through Databricks.
* Other enterprise data may remain in:
    * On-prem SQL Server
    * Azure SQL
    * Oracle
    * Salesforce
    * Other enterprise systems

The uploaded enterprise architecture diagram already reflects multiple enterprise source systems feeding the broader data platform.

The Citizen Developer interaction layer will be:

* Cloud CoWork
* Cloud Desktop
* Future MCP-compatible agents
* Future enterprise API consumers

Databricks UI, Genie UI, and Genie One UI are NOT part of the citizen-developer experience.

The citizen developer should never need to know whether the underlying data lives in Databricks, SQL Server, Azure SQL, or another system.

