15. Important LLM Architecture

The LLM/Genie must receive a bounded semantic context.

Do NOT send the entire enterprise catalog blindly to the LLM.

Flow:

User Question
|
v
Identity
|
v
Business Entitlement
|
v
Data Product
|
v
Relevant Semantic Context
|
v
LLM / Genie
|
v
Logical Query / SQL

The LLM is responsible for language/query interpretation.

The LLM is NOT responsible for authorization.

