16. Logical Query Model

Introduce a logical query abstraction where practical.

Do not make the entire internal architecture dependent on raw SQL.

Example:

{
“data_product”: “dental_claims”,
“metric”: “rejected_claims”,
“dimension”: “provider”,
“time_range”: “previous_month”
}

Then:

Logical Query
->
SQL generation
->
SQL Guardrails
->
Physical execution

This will make V2 multi-source support easier.

Do not over-engineer the logical query language in V1.

A simple Pydantic model is sufficient.

⸻

17. Data Source Abstraction

V1 must be source-agnostic by architecture.

Create:

DataSourceProvider

Interface.

Example:

DataSourceProvider
|
+– DatabricksProvider       <– V1 implementation
+– SQLServerProvider        <– future
+– AzureSQLProvider         <– future
+– OracleProvider           <– future
+– OtherProvider            <– future

Only implement Databricks in V1.

Do NOT implement SQL Server/Azure SQL now.

The purpose is to avoid coupling the entire system to Databricks.

