32. Semantic Discovery POC

For Dental, do NOT manually create a complete semantic model first.

Build a discovery process that reads available metadata and produces candidate semantics.

Example candidate:

{
“concept”: “claim”,
“source”: “catalog.schema.claims”,
“status”: “DISCOVERED”,
“confidence”: “HIGH”
}

Another:

{
“concept”: “rejected_claim”,
“source”: “catalog.schema.claims.claim_status”,
“condition”: “REJECTED”,
“status”: “DISCOVERED”,
“confidence”: “MEDIUM”
}

The discovery process must not automatically grant access.

Semantic discovery and authorization are completely separate.

⸻

