40. Final Architectural Principle

The product being built is NOT:

“An LLM that queries Databricks.”

The product is:

“An Enterprise Data Gateway that provides governed access to enterprise Data Products.”

Its responsibilities are:

Identity
+
Business Entitlement
+
Semantic Context
+
Query Understanding
+
SQL Guardrails
+
Query Planning
+
Source-specific Execution
+
Technical Authorization
+
Audit

Databricks is the primary V1 data platform.

Genie is the initial V1 query-understanding implementation.

OpenAI is a future interchangeable query-understanding implementation.

Unity Catalog is the technical security boundary for Databricks.

Cloud CoWork is the interaction layer.

The architecture must remain source-agnostic so that future versions can connect SQL Server, Azure SQL, Oracle, Salesforce, APIs, and other enterprise data sources without redesigning the Enterprise Data Gateway.
